<.shell title="Search" current={:search}>
  <h1>Search</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Find a team's members, activities, equipment, qualifications, groups, endorsements, templates, and pages from the top bar.
  </p>

  <h2>Results</h2>
  <p>
    What a team admin sees after typing "rope". The first result is highlighted: Enter opens it.
  </p>
  <div class="demo search-demo">
    <.search_box
      id="search-demo-results"
      query="rope"
      groups={sample_search_groups()}
      kinds={Web.Search.kinds(true, false)}
      team={sample_team()}
      open={true}
    />
  </div>

  <h3>Before typing</h3>
  <p>Says what this person can find. A member who logs in finds activities and pages only.</p>
  <div class="demo search-demo">
    <.search_box
      id="search-demo-empty"
      kinds={Web.Search.kinds(true, false)}
      team={sample_team()}
      open={true}
    />
  </div>

  <h3>Nothing found</h3>
  <div class="demo search-demo">
    <.search_box
      id="search-demo-none"
      query="cheakamus bridge"
      kinds={Web.Search.kinds(true, false)}
      team={sample_team()}
      open={true}
    />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      On a desktop the field sits in the <a href={page_path(:top_bar)}>top bar</a>
      before your initials. Select it, or press <kbd>/</kbd>
      anywhere, and the results open under it while the page dims. Arrow keys move, Enter opens, Esc closes.
    </li>
    <li>
      Below 1024px the bar has a magnifying glass instead. It opens a sheet over the whole page with the keyboard up, and Cancel closes it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Every word typed must match, in any order: a name or title, a D4H number, or an item's barcode or serial. Results come in groups of up to 5, the best group first.
    </li>
    <li>
      A result shows only when you can open its page. A member who logs in finds activities and their own pages.
    </li>
    <li>
      With more than 5 matches for one word, the group links to its list, filtered the same way.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>Web.Components.SearchBox</code>
    puts <code>&lt;.search_box&gt;</code>
    in the top bar on a team's pages and runs <code>Web.Search.run/3</code>
    as you type. What it matches is in <code>docs/search.md</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
